  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q2-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "True or False?",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p15-q2-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{x}{x+y}+\\frac{y}{x+y}=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True, for $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{x+y}+\\frac{y}{x+y}&=\\frac{x+y}{x+y}\\\\\\frac{x}{x+y}+\\frac{y}{x+y}&=1\\end{align*}$$\nTrue on the original domain $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q3-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\frac1x+\\frac1y=\\frac2{x+y}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. $\\frac1x+\\frac1y=\\frac{x+y}{xy}$.\n\nDomain: $x,y\\ne0$ and $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1x+\\frac1y&=\\frac{y}{xy}+\\frac{x}{xy}\\\\\\frac1x+\\frac1y&=\\frac{x+y}{xy}\\end{align*}$$\nFalse as an identity. Common domain: $x,y\\ne0$ and $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q4-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{2x+y}{x+y}+\\frac{x+2y}{x+y}=3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True, for $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x+y}{x+y}+\\frac{x+2y}{x+y}&=\\frac{3x+3y}{x+y}\\\\\\frac{2x+y}{x+y}+\\frac{x+2y}{x+y}&=\\frac{3(x+y)}{x+y}\\\\\\frac{2x+y}{x+y}+\\frac{x+2y}{x+y}&=3\\end{align*}$$\nTrue on the original domain $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q5-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{x^2-y^2}{x+y}=x-y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True, for $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-y^2}{x+y}&=\\frac{(x-y)(x+y)}{x+y}\\\\\\frac{x^2-y^2}{x+y}&=x-y\\end{align*}$$\nTrue on the original domain $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q6-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{x^2+y^2}{x+y}=x+y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. $(x+y)^2=x^2+2xy+y^2$.\n\nDomain: $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "For the proposed cancellation to hold as an identity, the numerator would need to equal $(x+y)^2$. However,\n$$(x+y)^2=x^2+2xy+y^2.$$\nThe $2xy$ term is missing from the printed numerator, so the statement is false. The original domain is $x+y\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\frac1x-\\frac1y=\\frac1{x-y}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. $\\frac1x-\\frac1y=\\frac{y-x}{xy}$. Domain: $x,y\\ne0$ and $x\\ne y$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1x-\\frac1y&=\\frac{y}{xy}-\\frac{x}{xy}\\\\\\frac1x-\\frac1y&=\\frac{y-x}{xy}\\end{align*}$$\nFalse as an identity. Common domain: $x,y\\ne0$ and $x\\ne y$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q8-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{x+y}{y}=\\frac xy+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True, for $y\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x+y}{y}&=\\frac xy+\\frac yy\\\\\\frac{x+y}{y}&=\\frac xy+1\\end{align*}$$\nTrue on the original domain $y\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q9-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\frac y{x+y}=\\frac1{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. The $y$ cannot cancel from only one denominator term. Common domain: $x+y\\ne0$, $x\\ne-1$.",
          "worked": "Cancellation must divide every term of the numerator and denominator by the same nonzero factor. When $y\\ne0$,\n$$\\frac y{x+y}=\\frac1{\\frac{x}{y}+1},$$\nnot generally $\\frac1{x+1}$. For example, $x=1$, $y=2$ gives $\\frac23$ on the left and $\\frac12$ on the right.\n\nThe statement is false. The common domain of the original printed sides is $x+y\\ne0$, $x\\ne-1$; $y=0$ is not excluded from that domain.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q10-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{2x-y}{x-y}-\\frac{x+2y}{x-y}=\\frac{x+y}{x-y}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. The left-hand side is $\\frac{x-3y}{x-y}$, where $x\\ne y$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x-y}{x-y}-\\frac{x+2y}{x-y}&=\\frac{2x-y-(x+2y)}{x-y}\\\\\\frac{2x-y}{x-y}-\\frac{x+2y}{x-y}&=\\frac{2x-y-x-2y}{x-y}\\\\\\frac{2x-y}{x-y}-\\frac{x+2y}{x-y}&=\\frac{x-3y}{x-y}\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract both terms of the second numerator. False as an identity; domain: $x\\ne y$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      }
    ]
  },
